note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note cbor.om: the CBOR (RFC 8949) subset that Tailscale Tailnet Lock (tka, tag v1.102.0) uses.
note Decoder: accepts and rejects exactly what github.com/fxamacker/cbor/v2 v2.9.0 Wellformed
note accepts and rejects under tka's cborDecOpts (tka/tka.go 23-32): no tags, no indefinite
note lengths, at most 16 nested arrays/maps, at most 4096 array elements, at most 1024 map pairs,
note no bytes after the item. Like fxamacker it is lenient about form: non-shortest heads and
note unsorted map keys are accepted (the encoder writes the canonical form). Floats and simple
note values are kept as opaque tokens. Duplicate keys and text UTF-8 are typed checks in
note fxamacker; cbrdupk and cbrutf8 are the helpers the model layer applies where Go does.
note Encoder: CTAP2 canonical as cbor.CTAP2EncOptions (encode.go 647-656): shortest heads,
note definite lengths, map keys sorted bytewise-lexically by their canonical encoding.
note Library unit: functions only, no main, no globals. Every name starts with cbr.
note Never traps on input bytes; traps only on caller contract violations (see README).
note NOT constant-time-audited.
note
note Token table t (ulong 131074): token i at t[2i] (argument) and t[2i+1] (packed):
note   bits 0..2 major type, bits 3..7 additional information (0..27),
note   bits 8..24 offset of the head in the input, bits 32..48 index of the token after the subtree.
note   t[131072] = token count, t[131073] = input length. Tokens are in input (pre-)order; the
note   items of an array or map follow its token; a map's items alternate key, value.
note Error codes of cbrdec (the class of the fxamacker error, in its check order, valid.go):
note   1 empty input            2 truncated               3 reserved additional information
note   4 indefinite length      5 break code outside one  6 tag
note   7 simple value < 32 in two bytes                     8 more than 16 nested arrays/maps
note   9 array over 4096        10 map over 1024 pairs    11 bytes after the item
note   12 length or count >= 2^63

note argument width in bytes for additional information a: 0 for a < 24, 1 2 4 8 for 24..27,
note 9 for the reserved 28..30 and the indefinite 31
fn cbrargw a ulong to ulong
if lt a 24
ret 0
end
if eq a 24
ret 1
end
if eq a 25
ret 2
end
if eq a 26
ret 4
end
if eq a 27
ret 8
end
ret 9
end

note big-endian unsigned value of d[p..p+w), w <= 8
fn cbrbe d view uchar 65536 p ulong w ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for k ulong w
v = or shl v 8 ulong get d add p k
end
ret v
end

note error for additional information 28..31 at depth dep (fxamacker valid.go 366-377, 110-114, 126-137)
fn cbrbadai m ulong a ulong dep ulong to ulong
if ne a 31
ret 3
end
if eq m 7
ret 5
end
if or eq m 2 eq m 3
ret 4
end
if or eq m 4 eq m 5
if ge dep 16
ret 8
end
ret 4
end
ret 3
end

note checks after the head (valid.go 108-210): q = offset after the head, dep = open containers
fn cbrargck n ulong q ulong m ulong v ulong dep ulong to ulong
if eq m 6
ret 6
end
if or eq m 2 eq m 3
if gt v 9223372036854775807
ret 12
end
if gt v sub n q
ret 2
end
ret 0
end
if or eq m 4 eq m 5
if ge dep 16
ret 8
end
if gt v 9223372036854775807
ret 12
end
if and eq m 4 gt v 4096
ret 9
end
if and eq m 5 gt v 1024
ret 10
end
end
ret 0
end

note argument of a head with additional information a and argument width w at d[p]
fn cbrhv d view uchar 65536 p ulong a ulong w ulong to ulong
if eq w 0
ret a
end
ret cbrbe d add p 1 w
end

fn cbrput t edit ulong 131074 i ulong v ulong x ulong to void
put t mul i 2 v
put t add mul i 2 1 x
end

note parse the head at d[p] into token i (dep containers open); 0 or an error code
fn cbrhd d view uchar 65536 n ulong p ulong t edit ulong 131074 i ulong dep ulong to ulong
if ge p n
ret 2
end
m = ulong shr get d p 5
a = ulong and get d p 31
w = cbrargw a
if gt w 8
ret cbrbadai m a dep
end
if gt add add p 1 w n
ret 2
end
v = cbrhv d p a w
if and eq m 7 and eq a 24 lt v 32
ret 7
end
cbrput t i v or or m shl a 3 shl p 8
ret cbrargck n add add p 1 w m v dep
end

note accessors of token i
fn cbrmaj t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
ret and get t add mul i 2 1 7
end

fn cbrai t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
ret and shr get t add mul i 2 1 3 31
end

fn cbrval t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
ret get t mul i 2
end

fn cbrhoff t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
ret and shr get t add mul i 2 1 8 131071
end

fn cbrnext t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
ret shr get t add mul i 2 1 32
end

fn cbrcount t view ulong 131074 to ulong
ret get t 131072
end

fn cbrinlen t view ulong 131074 to ulong
ret get t 131073
end

note offset of the payload of token i (the byte after its head)
fn cbrpoff t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
ret add add cbrhoff t i 1 cbrargw cbrai t i
end

note input offset just after token i's own bytes (head, plus payload for byte and text strings)
fn cbrtend t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
m = cbrmaj t i
if or eq m 2 eq m 3
ret add cbrpoff t i cbrval t i
end
ret cbrpoff t i
end

note number of items directly inside token i: array elements, or 2 per map pair
fn cbritems t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
m = cbrmaj t i
if eq m 4
ret cbrval t i
end
if eq m 5
ret mul cbrval t i 2
end
ret 0
end

note input bytes of the subtree of token i
fn cbrspan t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
nx = cbrnext t i
e = cbrinlen t
if lt nx cbrcount t
e = cbrhoff t nx
end
ret sub e cbrhoff t i
end

fn cbrsetn t edit ulong 131074 i ulong nx ulong to void
k = add mul i 2 1
put t k or get t k shl nx 32
end

note one item finished: count it off the open containers, closing every one that is now full;
note returns the new stack depth
fn cbrpop t edit ulong 131074 sk edit ulong 32 sr edit ulong 32 sp ulong nx ulong to ulong
s = sp
while gt s 0 bound 64
k = sub s 1
r = sub get sr k 1
put sr k r
if gt r 0
ret s
end
cbrsetn t get sk k nx
s = k
end
ret s
end

note decode d[0..n) into the token table t; 0 on success, else an error code (header notes).
note n > 65536 is a caller error: trap 3.
fn cbrdec d view uchar 65536 n ulong t edit ulong 131074 to ulong
if gt n 65536
trap 3
end
put t 131072 0
put t 131073 n
if eq n 0
ret 1
end
sk = new ulong 32 0
sr = new ulong 32 0
sp = ulong 0
i = ulong 0
p = ulong 0
while true bound 65537
e = cbrhd d n p t i sp
if ne e 0
ret e
end
p = cbrtend t i
c = cbritems t i
if gt c 0
put sk sp i
put sr sp c
sp = add sp 1
else
cbrsetn t i add i 1
sp = cbrpop t sk sr sp add i 1
end
i = add i 1
if eq sp 0
break
end
end
put t 131072 i
if ne p n
ret 11
end
ret 0
end

note value token of the first pair whose key is the unsigned integer key in map token m; 0 if none
note (0 is never a value token). Keys of other types are skipped.
fn cbrmfind t view ulong 131074 m ulong key ulong to ulong
k = add m 1
for j ulong cbrval t m
v = cbrnext t k
if and eq cbrmaj t k 0 eq cbrval t k key
ret v
end
k = cbrnext t v
end
ret 0
end

note 1 when byte or text tokens a and b hold the same bytes
fn cbrbeq d view uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 a ulong b ulong to ulong
if ne cbrval t a cbrval t b
ret 0
end
pa = cbrpoff t a
pb = cbrpoff t b
for k ulong cbrval t a
if ne get d add pa k get d add pb k
ret 0
end
end
ret 1
end

note integer key i as its int64 bit pattern (decode.go 2768-2784)
fn cbrkiv t view ulong 131074 i ulong to ulong
if eq cbrmaj t i 1
ret not cbrval t i
end
ret cbrval t i
end

note a negative integer key below -2^63 (an error in Go, decode.go 2773-2782)
fn cbrkbig t view ulong 131074 i ulong to bool
ret and eq cbrmaj t i 1 gt cbrval t i 9223372036854775807
end

note 1 when map keys a and b are the same key under fxamacker's duplicate rule (decode.go 2765-2815):
note integers compare as int64 (so 2^64-1 equals -1, as in Go); a negative integer below -2^63 is a
note decode error in Go and never equal here; strings compare type and bytes; simple values and
note floats compare head and argument; arrays and maps are never equal (Go rejects them as keys).
fn cbrkeq d view uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 a ulong b ulong to ulong
ma = cbrmaj t a
mb = cbrmaj t b
if and le ma 1 le mb 1
if or cbrkbig t a cbrkbig t b
ret 0
end
if eq cbrkiv t a cbrkiv t b
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
if ne ma mb
ret 0
end
if or eq ma 2 eq ma 3
ret cbrbeq d t a b
end
if and eq ma 7 and eq cbrval t a cbrval t b eq cbrai t a cbrai t b
ret 1
end
ret 0
end

note 1 when map token m has two keys equal under cbrkeq, else 0
fn cbrdupk d view uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 m ulong to ulong
np = cbrval t m
k = add m 1
for j ulong np
l = cbrnext t cbrnext t k
for x ulong sub sub np j 1
if eq cbrkeq d t k l 1
ret 1
end
l = cbrnext t cbrnext t l
end
k = cbrnext t cbrnext t k
end
ret 0
end

note second-byte range of a UTF-8 sequence led by b (Unicode 15 Table 3-7, as Go utf8.Valid)
fn cbru8lo b ulong to ulong
if eq b 224
ret 160
end
if eq b 240
ret 144
end
ret 128
end

fn cbru8hi b ulong to ulong
if eq b 237
ret 159
end
if eq b 244
ret 143
end
ret 191
end

note sequence length for lead byte b >= 128: 2 3 4, or 0 when b cannot lead
fn cbru8w b ulong to ulong
if and ge b 194 le b 223
ret 2
end
if and ge b 224 le b 239
ret 3
end
if and ge b 240 le b 244
ret 4
end
ret 0
end

note 1 when d[off..off+ln) is valid UTF-8 (Go utf8.Valid), else 0; off+ln > 65536 traps 3
fn cbrutf8 d view uchar 65536 off ulong ln ulong to ulong
i = ulong 0
while lt i ln bound 65537
b = ulong get d add off i
if lt b 128
i = add i 1
continue
end
w = cbru8w b
if or eq w 0 gt add i w ln
ret 0
end
c = ulong get d add add off i 1
if or lt c cbru8lo b gt c cbru8hi b
ret 0
end
for k ulong sub w 2
c = ulong get d add add off i add k 2
if or lt c 128 gt c 191
ret 0
end
end
i = add i w
end
ret 1
end

note shortest argument width for v: 0 (v < 24), 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes
fn cbrhw v ulong to ulong
if lt v 24
ret 0
end
if le v 255
ret 1
end
if le v 65535
ret 2
end
if le v 4294967295
ret 4
end
ret 8
end

note additional information for argument width w in 1 2 4 8
fn cbrwai w ulong to ulong
if eq w 1
ret 24
end
if eq w 2
ret 25
end
if eq w 4
ret 26
end
ret 27
end

note v as w big-endian bytes at o[q..q+w); returns q + w
fn cbrwbe o edit uchar 65536 q ulong v ulong w ulong to ulong
for k ulong w
put o add q k uchar and shr v mul sub sub w k 1 8 255
end
ret add q w
end

note write the shortest head for major m and argument v at o[q]; returns the offset after it.
note Not for floats (cbrtok writes those). Traps 3 when the head does not fit in o.
fn cbrhead o edit uchar 65536 q ulong m ulong v ulong to ulong
w = cbrhw v
if eq w 0
put o q uchar or shl m 5 v
ret add q 1
end
put o q uchar or shl m 5 cbrwai w
ret cbrwbe o add q 1 v w
end

note copy d[p..p+n) to o[q..q+n); returns q + n
fn cbrcopy d view uchar 65536 p ulong o edit uchar 65536 q ulong n ulong to ulong
for k ulong n
put o add q k get d add p k
end
ret add q n
end

note write token i of input d at o[q] in canonical form (strings with their payload); new offset.
note Simple values are canonical already (fxamacker rejects simple < 32 in two bytes); floats keep
note their width and bits.
fn cbrtok d view uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 i ulong o edit uchar 65536 q ulong to ulong
m = cbrmaj t i
v = cbrval t i
a = cbrai t i
if and eq m 7 ge a 25
put o q uchar add 224 a
ret cbrwbe o add q 1 v cbrargw a
end
r = cbrhead o q m v
if or eq m 2 eq m 3
ret cbrcopy d cbrpoff t i o r v
end
ret r
end

note bytes.Compare of o[a0..a1) and o[b0..b1) > 0
fn cbrkgt o view uchar 65536 a0 ulong a1 ulong b0 ulong b1 ulong to bool
la = sub a1 a0
lb = sub b1 b0
l = la
if lt lb l
l = lb
end
for k ulong l
x = get o add a0 k
y = get o add b0 k
if ne x y
ret gt x y
end
end
ret gt la lb
end

note Pair workspace w (ulong 4096) for one map of np <= 1024 pairs, in output offsets:
note   w[j] key start, w[1024+j] key end (value start), w[2048+j] pair end, w[3072+j] order.

note key of pair b sorts after key of pair c
fn cbrpgt o view uchar 65536 w view ulong 4096 b ulong c ulong to bool
ret cbrkgt o get w b get w add 1024 b get w c get w add 1024 c
end

note stable insertion sort of the order w[3072..3072+np) by key bytes o[w[x]..w[1024+x])
fn cbrisort o view uchar 65536 w edit ulong 4096 np ulong to void
for j ulong np
c = get w add 3072 j
s = j
while gt s 0 bound 1025
b = get w add 3071 s
if not cbrpgt o w b c
break
end
put w add 3072 s b
s = sub s 1
end
put w add 3072 s c
end
end

note rewrite o[w[0]..) with the pairs in sorted order; returns the end offset, which must be
note w[2048+np-1] (the caller traps 10 otherwise: an internal invariant, never seen in any run)
fn cbrperm o edit uchar 65536 w view ulong 4096 np ulong sc edit uchar 65536 to ulong
s = ulong 0
for j ulong np
b = get w add 3072 j
p = get w b
s = cbrcopy o p sc s sub get w add 2048 b p
end
ret cbrcopy sc 0 o get w 0 s
end

note store pair j of a map: key token k, value token v, next pair token l (output offsets oo[token])
fn cbrpset w edit ulong 4096 oo view ulong 65537 j ulong k ulong v ulong l ulong to void
put w j get oo k
put w add 1024 j get oo v
put w add 2048 j get oo l
put w add 3072 j j
end

note fill w for map token m
fn cbrpairs t view ulong 131074 m ulong oo view ulong 65537 w edit ulong 4096 to void
k = add m 1
for j ulong cbrval t m
v = cbrnext t k
l = cbrnext t v
cbrpset w oo j k v l
k = l
end
end

note sort the encoded pairs of map token m in place (w and sc are scratch, reused for every map)
fn cbrsortm o edit uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 m ulong oo view ulong 65537 w edit ulong 4096 sc edit uchar 65536 to void
np = cbrval t m
cbrpairs t m oo w
cbrisort o w np
if ne cbrperm o w np sc get w add 2047 np
trap 10
end
end

note pass 2 of cbrencs: sort every map with 2 or more pairs among tokens r..nx-1, last first
fn cbrsorts o edit uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 r ulong nx ulong oo view ulong 65537 to void
w = new ulong 4096 0
sc = new uchar 65536 0
i = nx
while gt i r bound 65537
i = sub i 1
if and eq cbrmaj t i 5 gt cbrval t i 1
cbrsortm o t i oo w sc
end
end
end

note encode the subtree of token r of input d (decoded into t by cbrdec) at o[off..), CTAP2
note canonical; returns the offset after it. The output is never longer than the input subtree
note (cbrspan); off + cbrspan t r > 65536 is a caller error: trap 9 before any write.
note Pass 1 writes every token in canonical form and records its output offset oo[token]; pass 2
note sorts the pairs of every map with 2 or more pairs, last token first, so a map's keys are
note final before the map that holds them is sorted. Sorting permutes bytes inside one map's
note range only, so the offset of every token that heads a pair of an enclosing map is unchanged.
fn cbrencs d view uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 r ulong o edit uchar 65536 off ulong to ulong
if gt add off cbrspan t r 65536
trap 9
end
nx = cbrnext t r
oo = new ulong 65537 0
q = off
i = r
while lt i nx bound 65537
put oo i q
q = cbrtok d t i o q
i = add i 1
end
put oo nx q
cbrsorts o t r nx oo
ret q
end

note canonical encoding of the whole decoded item into o; returns its length
fn cbrenc d view uchar 65536 t view ulong 131074 o edit uchar 65536 to ulong
ret cbrencs d t 0 o 0
end
